SUMMARY: Swing Dance with Dorian Mode
DESCRIPTION:Join us for SUNDAY SWING NIGHT at Hall of the Above\n\n🎷 Fea
 turing a new-to-HOTA band\, The doRiaN Mode! 🎷\n\nThe doRiaN Mode explor
 es the Great American Songbook as it dishes up vintage jazz\, swinging R&
 B\, and soulful ballads\, from the sounds of 1920s speakeasies and 1930s 
 big-band swing to 1940s jump blues and the rollicking R&B of Ruth Brown. 
 Vocalist and bassist Dorian Bartley leads this Petaluma-based acoustic qu
 artet featuring Robby Elfman on piano/clarinet\, Peter Graves on sax\, an
 d Tony Blake on drums. Whether they’re stomping at the Savoy in salute to
  Count Basie or paying homage to R&B legend Etta James\, the doRiaN Mode 
 brings elegance to classic American music.\n\n\n💃🏻 Jasmine Worrell\, th
 e Bay Area’s top swing dance instructor\, will offer a class from 4:15 – 
 5:00\n\n👯 Followed by live music and an open dance floor until 7:00 PM\n
 \n🎟️ $25 for admission includes the class — cash at the door. Kids 12 an
 d under are free.\n\n🕺🏾 All skill levels welcome\; no partner required.
 \n\n\nSee you on the dance floor!
CATEGORIES:petaluma,dance,swing,lesson
