SUMMARY: Theatre District Summer Concert Series – Clementine Darling
DESCRIPTION:Theatre District is thrilled to announce the return of its Su
 mmer Concert Series for 2026. Beginning in June and running through Septe
 mber\, the series features free live music every Friday from 6:00 PM to 8
 :00 PM in downtown Petaluma. The concert series brings together local tal
 ent and diverse musical styles\, creating a vibrant community gathering i
 n the heart of the Theatre District.\n\nClementine Darling https://www.fa
 cebook.com/ClementineDarlingMusic/ is performing from 6:00 to 8:00 in The
 atre Square. We hope to see you there!\n\nClementine Darling is a Sonoma 
 County–based Americana folk singer-songwriter known for her soulful story
 telling and “freak folk” sound that blends indie Americana with subtle 90
 ’s grunge influences. Originally from Seattle\, she busked her way down t
 he West Coast before settling in Northern California\, where she became a
  distinctive voice in the Bay Area music scene. Her music reflects a jour
 ney-driven spirit\, rooted in raw\, honest lyricism and intimate acoustic
  arrangements that feel both personal and cinematic. With performances at
  festivals such as The Emerald Cup\, SXSW\, and Railroad Square Music Fes
 tival\, Clementine Darling has built a reputation for captivating live sh
 ows that balance vulnerability with a grounded\, earthy energy.
CATEGORIES:Summer-Concert-Series,Theatre-District,Music,Live-Music
